    "['set policy-options policy-statement [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'router bgp 100', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'router bgp 100', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper BGP neighbor configuration to Cisco IOS:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 100\\n neighbor 2001:db8:11::1 remote-as 100\\n address-family ipv6 unicast\\n  neighbor 2001:db8:11::1 activate\\n exit-address-family\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco IOS:\\n1. The peer-as is specified in the 'router bgp' statement (100 in this case)\\n2. IPv6 BGP neighbors need explicit activation in the address-family\\n3. The Juniper 'type external' is implied by the different AS numbers (though in this specific case both ASes are 100, which would normally be iBGP in Cisco)\\n4. The import policy would need separate configuration in Cisco using route-maps or prefix-lists\", 'trans_template': 'router bgp 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 2001:db8:11::1 remote-as 100', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'neighbor 2001:db8:11::1 remote-as 100', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper BGP neighbor configuration to Cisco IOS:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 100\\n neighbor 2001:db8:11::1 remote-as 100\\n address-family ipv6 unicast\\n  neighbor 2001:db8:11::1 activate\\n exit-address-family\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco IOS:\\n1. The peer-as is specified in the 'router bgp' statement (100 in this case)\\n2. IPv6 BGP neighbors need explicit activation in the address-family\\n3. The Juniper 'type external' is implied by the different AS numbers (though in this specific case both ASes are 100, which would normally be iBGP in Cisco)\\n4. The import policy would need separate configuration in Cisco using route-maps or prefix-lists\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 2001:db8:11::1 remote-as 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'address-family ipv6 unicast', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's th