    "['term [parameter2] from protocol [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'route-map IMPORT_DIRECT permit 10', 'parent_command': ['router bgp 100'], 'root': 'router bgp 100', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper policy statement:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map IMPORT_DIRECT permit 10\\n match protocol connected\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- Juniper's `policy-statement` translates to Cisco's `route-map`\\n- The `term 1` becomes the sequence number `10` (Cisco typically uses multiples of 10)\\n- `from protocol direct` in Juniper matches directly connected routes, which is `connected` in Cisco\\n- The implicit `then accept` in Juniper becomes `permit` in the route-map statement\", 'trans_template': 'route-map IMPORT_DIRECT permit 10'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'match protocol connected', 'parent_command': ['router bgp 100'], 'root': 'router bgp 100', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper policy statement:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map IMPORT_DIRECT permit 10\\n match protocol connected\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- Juniper's `policy-statement` translates to Cisco's `route-map`\\n- The `term 1` becomes the sequence number `10` (Cisco typically uses multiples of 10)\\n- `from protocol direct` in Juniper matches directly connected routes, which is `connected` in Cisco\\n- The implicit `then accept` in Juniper becomes `permit` in the route-map statement\", 'trans_template': 'match protocol connected'}]]": 1,
